        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set provides a strategic list of seven highly fertile research avenues within the fields of **Cosmology, Stellar Astrophysics, and Galactic/Planetary Science**. Each topic is intentionally framed to facilitate a rigorous, multi-faceted academic exploration, specifically designed to address the complex prompt structure of *Historical Context, Foundational Principles, Mechanisms & Processes, Evidence & Manifestations,* and *Broader Implications*. The topics focus on the dynamic *interactions* between cosmic components—such as the role of Dark Matter in structure formation, the feedback loop between Black Holes and galaxies, or the bi-directional influence between exoplanet detection biases and our understanding of planetary system diversity. These are not simple questions but complex relationships ripe for deep analysis.",
