        },
        {
          "text": "**Weak Gravitational Lensing:** A methodology for mapping the distribution of Dark Matter, which warps the light from background galaxies.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 100,
          "source": "topic-set-astrophysics-and-cosmology-🆔20251026011254.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**The Sunyaev-Zel'dovich Effect:** A phenomenon that allows for the detection of massive galaxy clusters through the scattering of CMB photons.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 103,
          "source": "topic-set-astrophysics-and-cosmology-🆔20251026011254.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Redshift-Space Distortions (RSDs):** A technique used in large-scale galaxy surveys to disentangle the effects of cosmological expansion from the peculiar motions of galaxies caused by local gravity.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 103,
          "source": "topic-set-astrophysics-and-cosmology-🆔20251026011254.md"
        },
        {
          "text": "**Planetary Migration Theory:** The mechanisms (e.g., disc-planet interaction) that explain why many exoplanets, like \"Hot Jupiters,\" are found in orbits that challenge classical in-situ formation models.",
          "indent_level": 1,
          "line_number": 114,
          "source": "topic-set-astrophysics-and-cosmology-🆔20251026011254.md"
        }
      ]
